## 23. Summary

Most MCP SDK 1.x error-handling recommendations remain valid when FastMCP 3.4.5 is added.

The primary difference is responsibility.

Without FastMCP:

```text
Application
      ↓
MCP SDK
```

With FastMCP:

```text
Application
      ↓
FastMCP
      ↓
MCP SDK
```

Therefore expected tool failures should generally follow:

```text
Expected Failure
      ↓
Application Error
      ↓
FastMCP ToolError
      ↓
MCP Tool Error
```

Dependency failures should follow:

```text
Dependency Failure
      ↓
Normalize
      ↓
Application Error
      ↓
Bounded Retry
      ↓
Retry Exhausted
      ↓
ToolError
```

Unexpected internal failures should follow:

```text
Unexpected Exception
      ↓
Full Server Logging
      ↓
Correlation ID
      ↓
Sanitization
      ↓
Safe Client Error
```

The core recommendation is:

> **Use FastMCP as the MCP-facing error adapter, not as the application's business error model.**

The preferred architecture is:

```text
Raw Exception
      ↓
Application Error
      ↓
Classification
      ↓
